   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to extending the authority of Chenango county to impose additional taxes",
    "basePrintNo": "S2181",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S2181-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1210, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S2181\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to extending the authority of\nChenango county to impose additional taxes\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nRelates to extending the authority of Chenango County to impose\nadditional taxes.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Clause 24 of subparagraph\n\n(i) of the opening paragraph of section 1210 of the tax law, as\namended by chapter 107 of the laws of 2013, is amended to read as\nfollows:\n\n(24) the county of Chenango is hereby further authorized and empowered\nto adopt and amend local laws, ordinances or resolutions imposing such\ntaxes at a rate which is one percent additional to the three percent\nrate authorized above in this paragraph for such county for the period\nbeginning September 1, 2002 and ending November 30, 2017.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nChenango County has requested that the New York State Legislature\nadopt an amendment to the Tax Law extending the authorization to\nimpose the additional one percent sales and compensating use tax.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
